          "summary": "The paper proposes FlipDir, a training-free inference-time method that estimates a low-rank flip-inducing activation subspace from contrastive pairs of original and answer-flipping inputs and selectively steers hidden states during decoding, with a margin-based gate limiting attenuation to uncertain steps so stable predictions are preserved. It also introduces VisFlip, a benchmark spanning nine dataset-variation combinations across scientific reasoning, robot-scene understanding, and medical VQA, where FlipDir outperforms existing methods on the combined recovery and preservation metric across 18 settings.",
