          "summary": "The paper proposes M²PFN, which turns the frozen tabular foundation model TabPFN into a multimodal Alzheimer's disease predictor by back-propagating task gradients through its transformer into 3D-MRI and tabular encoders, aligning the modalities into a shared subspace via disentanglement and a contrastive objective matched to the in-context-learning prior, and adding a learnable gated tabular-only shortcut. On ADNI it reaches 65.55% macro-F1 and 82.21% macro-AUC, and it achieves the best AUC and lowest MMSE MAE on two external cohorts without retraining.",
