          "summary": "The paper introduces RECLAIM, a benchmark of 100 NeurIPS 2025 papers in which an agent must reproduce a result fixed in advance, under a fixed GPU-hour budget, using the paper and whatever its authors released; difficulty tiers depend on those releases, and a separate language model grades runs from logs and outputs. Running four agents once per paper, the best agent in each tier reproduces only 41% of Run-tier papers, 27% at Retrain, and 15% at Reimplement.",
